radv: present Metal surfaces through the GPU's display engine on mac_linuxgpu

On mac_linuxgpu the GPU drives its own monitor: the driver runs a display
output that mirrors the macOS desktop to it and is the only one that
commits to it, and its libdrm (libdrm-mlg) lets a client put framebuffers
of the GPU's primary node on that output's planes (drmMlgScanout). RADV's
images then go straight to scanout, with no copy and without the Apple
GPU or the macOS compositor, whatever window the application presents
from.

- RADV advertises VK_EXT_metal_surface, and the surface and swapchain
  extensions, on the macOS platform; also VK_MVK_macos_surface, which
  SDL2 before 2.26 requires of a Vulkan library (Quake3e bundles 2.24.1).
  Its surfaces (an NSView backed by a CAMetalLayer, or the layer) are
  Metal surfaces.
- wsi_common_metal.c: a driver that is neither software nor Metal (RADV)
  presents its Metal surfaces through the display engine when libdrm
  defines LIBDRM_MLG_SCANOUT. Other drivers are unchanged.
- That presentation (the end of wsi_common_metal.c): MLG_WSI_OUTPUT names the output's connector (or
  "auto"); without it the surface reports no presentation support. The
  swapchain attaches to the output, makes its images framebuffers of the
  primary node with modifiers both of the output's planes scan out, and
  checks the first one with the driver. Each present is placed by
  libdrm-mlg's drmMlgPlaceWindow from the window's content and the
  monitor's screen in global points: the primary plane when the window
  fills that screen, else an overlay plane at the window's rectangle in
  CRTC pixels, clipped to the CRTC with the matching crop of the image,
  following the window frame by frame. A window off the monitor (or with
  less of it there than DC's smallest viewport) takes the frames off
  (LX_SCANOUT HIDE): the desktop shows, the game goes on paced at the
  refresh rate, and the frames come back with the window. A new place is
  checked by the driver before it is used; a refusal names the place and
  the scale. MLG_WSI_MODE=fullscreen or windowed decides instead of the
  window, and a layer at another size than the images makes presents
  return VK_SUBOPTIMAL_KHR. FIFO: every frame
  is shown, the next one handed over once the previous reached the screen;
  a per-image syncobj signals at the vblank that shows it, which acquire
  and VK_KHR_present_wait wait on. The last swapchain of the process gives
  the screen back to the desktop. Failures name the step and the errno on
  stderr and lose the surface.
- wsi_common_metal_layer.m: the layer's window and screen, read on the
  main thread; the window is moved to the monitor's screen at swapchain
  creation.
- meson: the frameworks the Metal WSI uses (AppKit now too) linked into
  whatever links the WSI.

